01:03:12,000 --> 01:03:18,000
There Will Be Blood is a 2007 American epic period drama film co-produced, written and
directed by Paul Thomas Anderson, loosely based on the 1927 novel Oil!

13
01:08:28,000 --> 01:08:34,000
by Upton Sinclair.

14
01:13:44,000 --> 01:13:50,000
It stars Daniel Day-Lewis, Paul Dano, Kevin J.

15
01:19:00,000 --> 01:19:06,000
O'Connor, Ciarán Hinds, and Dillon Freasier.

16
01:24:16,000 --> 01:24:22,000
The film follows silver miner-turned-oilman Daniel Plainview (Day-Lewis) as he embarks on a ruthless
quest for wealth during the Californian oil boom in the late 19th and early 20th centuries.

17
01:29:32,000 --> 01:29:38,000
Development on There Will Be Blood began after writer Eric Schlosser
purchased the film rights to Sinclair's novel in 2004.

18
01:34:48,000 --> 01:34:54,000
It was acquired by Ghoulardi Film Company, Paramount Vantage and Miramax Films
after Anderson completed the first draft of the film's screenplay.

19
01:40:04,000 --> 01:40:10,000
Day-Lewis immediately joined the project while Dano, who initially signed on for a smaller
role, took on a starring role after replacing Kel O'Neill during filming.

20
01:45:20,000 --> 01:45:26,000
Principal photography began in June 2006 and lasted until that September,
with filming locations including Los Angeles and Marfa, Texas.

21
01:50:36,000 --> 01:50:42,000
The film's music was composed by Radiohead guitarist Jonny Greenwood.

22
01:55:52,000 --> 01:55:58,000
There Will Be Blood premiered at Fantastic Fest in Austin on September 29, 2007.

23
02:01:08,000 --> 02:01:14,000
It was first theatrically released in New York City and Los Angeles on December
26 and in selected international markets on January 25, 2008.

24
02:06:24,000 --> 02:06:30,000
It grossed $76.1 million worldwide and received acclaim from critics, with praise for the
cinematography, Anderson's direction, screenplay, music, and performances of Day-Lewis and Dano.

25
02:11:40,000 --> 02:11:46,000
The National Board of Review, the American Film Institute and the National Society of
Film Critics named There Will Be Blood one of the top-ten films of 2007.

26
02:16:56,000 --> 02:17:02,000
The film was nominated for eight awards at the 80th Academy Awards, winning two (Best Actor for
Day-Lewis and Best Cinematography for Elswit) and received numerous other accolades.

27
02:22:12,000 --> 02:22:18,000
It has since been widely regarded as Paul Thomas Anderson's magnum opus, as well
as one of the greatest films of the 21st century and of all time.

28
02:27:28,000 --> 02:27:34,000
The film explores themes of california, petrol, sibling
relationship, based on novel or book, capitalism.

29
02:32:44,000 --> 02:32:50,000
The tone is emotional and thought_provoking.
